From 350ac8fedba518dc9fdb0a95795400336f28073e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:03:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: CI-run progress reads GitHub through the
 broker prefix

The CI-run progress check (#1956) ran `gh api` with no credential prefix. On the hub
`gh` has no login and the gateway env has no GH_TOKEN, so every read exited 4 and failed
open as `unknown`: the check never refused a park on an unstartable run and never woke
a card parked on one (self-heal agent-c2b8fc1abf; verify card t_01a1d3aae49cdabe). The
same call under the hub's `kanban.pr_acceptance.gh_command_prefix`
(`token-broker exec --scope user/github ... --`) exits 0.

- New `hermes_cli/kanban_gh_argv.dispatcher_gh_argv()`: `[*gh_command_prefix(None), gh]`,
  raising `GhArgvUnavailable` with fixed text (config errors may carry credentials).
  The dispatcher PR-state read (`_gh_argv`) and `_fetch_jobs` both use it.
- `_fetch_jobs` classifies gh exit 4, HTTP 401, a missing gh and an unbuildable argv as
  `NoCredential`; `Progress.no_credential` marks the fail-open.
- The sweep logs one WARNING per hour per process for that case ("gh api exit 4 ...;
  no credential: CI-run progress check disabled"), instead of a per-card line that
  hid a check disabled everywhere.

Proof:
- RED (before the `_fetch_jobs` change): test_run_read_goes_through_the_configured_broker_prefix
  got Progress(state='unknown', detail='gh api exit 4: To get started with GitHub CLI ...');
  GREEN: not_starting with labels self-hosted,ci-fast.
- 9/9 mutants killed (prefix dropped, gh-missing check, exit-4 / 401 classification,
  rate limit removed / never re-warn, sweep warn dropped, config-text leak, flag unset).
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress.py, test_kanban_park_invariants.py,
  test_kanban_dependency_review_relink.py, test_kanban_active_pr_foreign_contract.py,
  test_subprocess_text_encoding.py, test_subprocess_env_guard.py: green.

Undo: git revert <this commit>.
